239,"well_id":"MRN-17","depth_m":706.0,"formation":"Dhekiajuli","event_type":"Tight Hole","severity":"Low","severity_rank":0,"npt_hours":1.9,"mud_weight_ppg":9.2,"description":"Drag increased to 47 klbs at 706 m MD across Dhekiajuli clays; back-reamed to shoe.","mitigation":"Performed wiper trip to shoe and drilled ahead with increased YP mud.","lesson_learned":"Inhibitive mud is mandatory across Dhekiajuli reactive clays.","source_doc":"WCR MRN-17","event_date":"2023-06-10","origin":"seed","document_id":null,"citation":"MRN-17 · 706 m"},{"id":240,"well_id":"MRN-17","depth_m":1022.0,"formation":"Dhekiajuli","event_type":"Mud Loss","severity":"Low","severity_rank":0,"npt_hours":0.5,"mud_weight_ppg":9.1,"description":"Partial losses of 4 bbl/hr observed while drilling Dhekiajuli at 1,022 m MD with 9.1 ppg mud. Pit volume decreased 16 bbl before losses were controlled.","mitigation":"Pumped 42 ppb LCM pill (fine/medium) and reduced flow rate to lower ECD; losses cured after 2.3 hrs.","lesson_learned":"Reduce ECD (lower flow, controlled ROP) when approaching the Dhekiajuli loss zone.","source_doc":"WCR MRN-17","event_date":"2023-06-25","origin":"seed","document_id":null,"citation":"MRN-17 · 1,022 m"},{"id":241,"well_id":"MRN-17","depth_m":2293.0,"formation":"Tipam","event_type":"Mud Loss","severity":"Medium","severity_rank":1,"npt_hours":7.8,"mud_weight_ppg":10.0,"description":"Seepage to partial losses (28 bbl/hr) encountered in Tipam sands at 2,293 m MD; total loss 112 bbl.","mitigation":"Staged LCM (calcium carbonate + fibre) and drilled ahead at reduced pump rate with continuous pit monitoring.","lesson_learned":"Reduce ECD (lower flow, controlled ROP) when approaching the Tipam loss zone.","source_doc":"WCR MRN-17","event_date":"2023-08-29","origin":"seed","document_id":null,"citation":"MRN-17 · 2,293 m"},{"id":242,"well_id":"MRN-17","depth_m":2799.0,"formation":"Barail","event_type":"Stuck Pipe","severity":"High","severity_rank":2,"npt_hours":24.9,"mud_weight_ppg":10.3,"description":"Pipe became stuck while making connection at 2,799 m MD in Barail. Overpull to 93 klbs, no rotation. Torque had risen from 12.0 to 18.6 kft-lb over the preceding 60 m.","mitigation":"Applied controlled overpull to 93 klbs, spotted pipe-freeing agent and regained rotation after 9.9 hrs.","lesson_learned":"Rising torque trend in upper Barail is a precursor to stuck pipe; ream every stand and keep jars armed.","source_doc":"DDR MRN-17 · 2023-09-26","event_date":"2023-09-26","origin":"seed","document_id":null,"citation":"MRN-17 · 2,799 m"},{"id":243,"well_id":"MRN-17","depth_m":2816.0,"formation":"Barail","event_type":"Torque Spike","severity":"Medium","severity_rank":1,"npt_hours":5.6,"mud_weight_ppg":10.6,"description":"Torque spike to 16.9 kft-lb at 2,816 m MD (Barail); string stalled twice before parameters were reduced.","mitigation":"Lowered RPM, added lubricant to mud system and reamed the interval before drilling ahead.","lesson_learned":"Wiper trips every 150 m in Barail reduce pack-off and torque spikes.","source_doc":"DDR MRN-17 · 2023-09-27","event_date":"2023-09-27","origin":"seed","document_id":null,"citation":"MRN-17 · 2,816 m"},{"id":244,"well_id":"MRN-17","depth_m":2986.0,"formation":"Barail","event_type":"Wellbore Instability","severity":"Critical","severity_rank":3,"npt_hours":38.5,"mud_weight_ppg":10.8,"description":"Hole enlargement indicated by caliper across Barail at 2,986 m MD; MW 10.8 ppg considered marginal.","mitigation":"Circulated at higher rate to clear cavings and drilled ahead with improved rheology.","lesson_learned":"Slightly higher MW in Barail reduces cavings without inducing losses.","source_doc":"WCR MRN-17","event_date":"2023-10-06","origin":"seed","document_id":null,"citation":"MRN-17 · 2,986 m"},{"id":245,"well_id":"MRN-17","depth_m":3368.0,"formation":"Kopili","event_type":"Kick","severity":"Low","severity_rank":0,"npt_hours":1.2,"mud_weight_ppg":13.0,"description":"Drilling break followed by 14 bbl pit gai